<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Britain=E2=80=99s banks may be =E2=80=9Cpa=
rt of the jewel=E2=80=9D in the UK economic crown, as the chancellor, John =
Healey, <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_Jk=
LMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEAX2I5fp6olyh5yUeClMls_oO81-uKxH5qD9OgE=
-OcfN1V2E45Gw6za9diwWwlYdZtvZesieVBYv-UP2JWHQRUjWd0AvqFjUcEkdB1LndIOZMDju6_=
oSdyStNYD-Yesf6fe2A_dgFYcjRXohraPYzFcz1KzsY_hcHN_i8tfnluQsWKChBBMoD1B_Woiub=
-QuMd4Ct-fUEHTOXghwGIp4G12pjkmWwCxSRgCVIwpr534Z46HCt3romZ1XjlLo9cnaXAxwn7Qd=
JWElOFMfalEg9bVPto5ShRlNKMxP3uMW_TzlA/4ux/-tpfaRRwQX68HgexPRRztQ/h30/h001.n=
81N2IdD5uJcr0mZgZyf2oJyQLDU5Qt9WEjZHRmpHNk" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">put i=
t yesterday</a>, but that will not protect them from being hit in this mont=
h=E2=80=99s budget.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">John Healey is poised to raise the tax tak=
e from Britain=E2=80=99s banks in his 28 October budget, the Guardian under=
stands, as the chancellor looks to fix the damage inflicted on the public f=
inances by war in the Middle East.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">He has decided to tap the financial sector=
 for additional revenue.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">One option understood to be under discussi=
on =E2=80=93 reversing cuts to the bank surcharge made by Jeremy Hunt =E2=
=80=93 would raise upwards of =C2=A32bn a year.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Industry figures believe that will probabl=
y mean raising the surcharge back to 8%, from 3% at present, to help bolste=
r the government=E2=80=99s fiscal headroom (which has been eroded by the ju=
mp in borrowing costs this year).</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Shares in UK banks are dropping at the sta=
rt of trading, as investors react to the news about Healey=E2=80=99s budget=
.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Lloyds Banking Group is the top faller on =
the FTSE 100, down about 1.9%, with NatWest dropping by 1.6%.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">News of the looming tax raid came hours af=
ter Healey praised the banks as crucial to supporting economic growth, tell=
ing reporters: =E2=80=9CPeople too often see them as big, distant financial=
 institutions, when they are hardwired into the economic fabric of this cou=
ntry and our future prospects.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The Confederation of British Industry has =
said Healey should avoid =E2=80=9Cfurther sector-specific taxation=E2=80=9D=
, such as a bank tax.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Louise Hellem, the chief economist at the =
CBI, said: =E2=80=9CThe financial services sector is vital to driving inves=
tment, innovation and business growth across the economy. Government has se=
t the right direction through its Financial Services Growth and Competitive=
ness Strategy and the Leeds Reforms =E2=80=93 the priority now is delivery.=
</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=80=9CThe autumn budget should set the =
agenda for a competitive and predictable environment that turns those refor=
ms into tangible progress, unlocking domestic investment, deepening UK capi=
tal markets and helping more firms to scale and grow.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=80=9CIt should also avoid measures tha=
t would undermine competitiveness or weaken incentives to invest. With the =
business tax contribution already at a record share of receipts, that means=
 avoiding further sector-specific taxation, including on a banking sector a=
lready facing a higher tax rate than competing international financial cent=
res.=E2=80=9D</p>
